IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PARTS 6A, 7 AND 8, SECTIONS 66A TO 75 (part-time employees,
-- domestic workers, children and young persons).  Part ea2.
-- Source text: inputs/EmA1968.txt (a converter rendering, not the official text).
--
-- Notes for the reader.
--   * The keel's definitional answers are taken as MAYBE inputs named `the answer of s 2(1) "<term>"`.
--   * Ages are completed years.  "has not completed his or her 15th year of age" is read as: age under 15 (fork F13).
--   * Sections 66B, 70, 71(1) and the regulation-making half of s 73 are powers to make regulations or orders; they
--     have no function here (NOTES.md, Coverage).  What an order or regulation says arrives as an input
--     (for example `the minimum rate of salary prescribed by the order` in s 71(2)).
--   * A plain BOOLEAN or NUMBER answer is a date or count comparison and carries no legal "no".

§ `Part 6A -- part-time employees (s 66A)`

-- s 66A(1): "In this Part, 'part-time employee' means an employee who is required under his or her contract
-- of service with an employer to work for less than 35 hours a week."
-- src:2603 | 66A.—(1) In this Part, “part-time employee” means an employee
-- src:2604 | who is required under his or her contract of service with an employer
-- src:2605 | to work for less than 35 hours a week.
@ref s 66A(1) (src:2603-2605)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2(1) "employee"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the hours a week the employee is required to work under the contract of service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66A(1) the person is a part-time employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 2(1) "employee"`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the hours a week the employee is required to work under the contract of service` LESS THAN 35
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an employee who is required under his or her contract of service"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an employee who is required under his or her contract of service"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an employee is the answer of s 2(1) "employee", which the Act did not give on these facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 66A(2): "Despite subsection (1), the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, declare that any
-- employee or class of employees are not to be regarded as part-time employees for the purposes of this Part."
-- src:2607 | (2) Despite subsection (1), the Minister may, by notification in the
-- src:2608 | Gazette, declare that any employee or class of employees are not to be
-- src:2609 | regarded as part‑time employees for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 66A(2) (src:2607-2609)
GIVEN `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette declared that the employee or the employee's class is not to be regarded as part-time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66A(2) the employee is regarded as a part-time employee for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette declared that the employee or the employee's class is not to be regarded as part-time`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are not to be regarded as part-time employees for the purposes of this Part"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only takes an employee or class out; it does not make anyone a part-time employee
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 66A(1) and (2) gathered by hand (E1 option B; fork F8): a declaration under (2) wins over the definition in (1).
-- src:2603 | 66A.—(1) In this Part, “part-time employee” means an employee
-- src:2604 | who is required under his or her contract of service with an employer
-- src:2605 | to work for less than 35 hours a week.
-- src:2607 | (2) Despite subsection (1), the Minister may, by notification in the
-- src:2608 | Gazette, declare that any employee or class of employees are not to be
-- src:2609 | regarded as part‑time employees for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 66A(1) (src:2603-2609)
@ref s 66A(2) (src:2607-2609)
GIVEN `the answer of s 66A(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 66A(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66A(1) gathered with (2): the employee is a part-time employee for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are not to be regarded as part-time employees for the purposes of this Part"
        IF `the answer of s 66A(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the answer of s 66A(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an employee who is required under his or her contract of service"
        IF `the answer of s 66A(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): neither subsection answers
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Part 7 -- domestic workers (s 67)`

-- s 67: "The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, apply all or any of the provisions of this Act with
-- such modification as may be set out in the notification to all domestic workers or to any group, class or
-- number of domestic workers".  The provision applies to a domestic worker only if the Minister has applied it.
-- The regulation-making half of the section is a power and has no function here.
-- src:2624 | 67. The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, apply all or
-- src:2625 | any of the provisions of this Act with such modification as may be set
-- src:2626 | out in the notification to all domestic workers or to any group, class or
-- src:2627 | number of domestic workers and may make regulations to provide
-- src:2628 | generally for the engagement and working conditions of domestic
-- src:2629 | workers.
@ref s 67 (src:2624-2629)
GIVEN `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette applied the provision to all domestic workers or to a group, class or number that includes the domestic worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67 the provision of the Act applies to the domestic worker` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette applied the provision to all domestic workers or to a group, class or number that includes the domestic worker`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section says the Minister may apply the Act to domestic workers; it does not say that the Act does not apply to them until he does
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 8 -- children and young persons (ss 67A to 75)`

-- s 67A "child": "a person who has not completed his or her 15th year of age".
-- src:2634 | 67A. In this Part —
-- src:2636 | “child” means a person who has not completed his or her
-- src:2637 | 15th year of age;
@ref s 67A "child" (src:2634-2637)
GIVEN `the age of the person in completed years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67A "child" the person is a child` MEANS
    IF `the age of the person in completed years` LESS THAN 15
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a person who has not completed his or her 15th year of age"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 67A "young person": "a person who has completed his or her 15th year of age but who has not completed his or her 16th year of age".
-- src:2642 | “young person” means a person who has completed his or her
-- src:2643 | 15th year of age but who has not completed his or her
-- src:2644 | 16th year of age.
@ref s 67A "young person" (src:2642-2644)
GIVEN `the age of the person in completed years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67A "young person" the person is a young person` MEANS
    IF `the age of the person in completed years` AT LEAST 15 AND `the age of the person in completed years` LESS THAN 16
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a person who has completed his or her 15th year of age"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 72(1): "Sections 68 and 69 do not apply (a) to the employment of children and young persons (i) in work
-- approved and supervised by the Ministry of Education or the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore; and
-- (ii) carried on in any technical, vocational or industrial training school or institute; and (b) to the
-- employment of young persons under any apprenticeship programme approved and supervised by the Institute of
-- Technical Education, Singapore."  Answers whether sections 68 and 69 apply: NO for the two cases, else NOTHING.
-- src:2700 | 72.—(1) Sections 68 and 69 do not apply —
-- src:2702 | (a) to the employment of children and young persons —
-- src:2704 | (i) in work approved and supervised by the Ministry of
-- src:2705 | Education or the Institute of Technical Education,
-- src:2706 | Singapore; and
-- src:2708 | (ii) carried on in any technical, vocational or industrial
-- src:2709 | training school or institute; and
-- src:2711 | (b) to the employment of young persons under any
-- src:2712 | apprenticeship programme approved and supervised by
-- src:2713 | the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore.
@ref s 72(1) (src:2700-2713)
GIVEN `the person is a young person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the work is approved and supervised by the Ministry of Education or the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is carried on in a technical, vocational or industrial training school or institute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is under an apprenticeship programme approved and supervised by the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(1) sections 68 and 69 apply to the employment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sections 68 and 69 do not apply"
        IF `the work is approved and supervised by the Ministry of Education or the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore`
           AND `the work is carried on in a technical, vocational or industrial training school or institute`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sections 68 and 69 do not apply"
        IF `the person is a young person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the employment is under an apprenticeship programme approved and supervised by the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 72 takes only the employment it describes out of sections 68 and 69
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 72(2): "the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore means the Institute of Technical Education,
-- Singapore established under the Institute of Technical Education Act 1992."
-- src:2715 | (2) For the purposes of this section, the Institute of Technical
-- src:2716 | Education, Singapore means the Institute of Technical Education,
-- src:2717 | Singapore established under the Institute of Technical Education
-- src:2718 | Act 1992.
@ref s 72(2) (src:2715-2718)
GIVEN `the body was established under the Institute of Technical Education Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(2) the body is the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the body was established under the Institute of Technical Education Act 1992`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore means the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore established under the Institute of Technical Education Act 1992"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 68(2): "A child may be employed in an industrial undertaking in which only members of the same family are employed."
-- src:2652 | (2) A child may be employed in an industrial undertaking in which
-- src:2653 | only members of the same family are employed.
@ref s 68(2) (src:2652-2653)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2(1) "industrial undertaking"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `only members of the same family are employed in the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(2) a child may be employed in the undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 2(1) "industrial undertaking"` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `only members of the same family are employed in the undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection permits employment in an industrial undertaking in which only members of the same family are employed
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 68(4): "For the purposes of subsection (3), the certificate of a medical officer is conclusive upon the
-- question of whether any work is suited to the capacity of any particular child."
-- src:2659 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), the certificate of a medical
-- src:2660 | officer is conclusive upon the question of whether any work is suited
-- src:2661 | to the capacity of any particular child.
@ref s 68(4) (src:2659-2661)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2(1) "medical officer"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the certificate says the work is suited to the capacity of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(4) the work is suited to the capacity of the child` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 2(1) "medical officer"`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the certificate says the work is suited to the capacity of the child`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only the certificate "of a medical officer" is conclusive, and the certifier is not one
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the certifier is a medical officer is the answer of s 2(1) "medical officer", which the Act did not give on these facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 68(3): "A child who is 13 years of age or above may be employed in light work suited to his or her
-- capacity in a non-industrial undertaking."  "Non-industrial" is "not an industrial undertaking"; on the keel's
-- reading of "industrial undertaking" (finding F3) every undertaking is industrial, so the seat asks directly.
-- src:2655 | (3) A child who is 13 years of age or above may be employed in
-- src:2656 | light work suited to his or her capacity in a non‑industrial
-- src:2657 | undertaking.
@ref s 68(3) (src:2655-2657)
GIVEN `the age of the child in completed years` IS A NUMBER
      `the answer of s 2(1) "industrial undertaking"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the work is light work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 68(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(3) a child may be employed in the undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the age of the child in completed years` AT LEAST 13
       AND `the answer of s 2(1) "industrial undertaking"` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       AND `the work is light work`
       AND `the answer of s 68(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection permits a child aged 13 or above in light work suited to his or her capacity in a non-industrial undertaking
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 68(1): "A person must not employ a child in an industrial or a non-industrial undertaking except as
-- provided for in subsections (2) and (3)."  Section 72 takes some employment out of the section.
-- src:2648 | 68.—(1) A person must not employ a child in an industrial or a
-- src:2649 | non‑industrial undertaking except as provided for in subsections (2)
-- src:2650 | and (3).
@ref s 68(1) (src:2648-2650)
GIVEN `the answer of s 67A "child"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 68(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 68(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 72(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(1) the person may employ the child` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks of a child
        IF `the answer of s 67A "child"` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a child is the answer of s 67A "child", which was not given
        IF `the answer of s 67A "child"` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 72(1) says sections 68 and 69 do not apply to this employment
        IF `the answer of s 72(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
        IF `the answer of s 68(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of s 68(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person must not employ a child in an industrial or a non-industrial undertaking"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 69: "A young person must not be employed in any industrial undertaking which the Minister by notification
-- in the Gazette declares to be an industrial undertaking in which a young person must not be employed."
-- src:2665 | 69. A young person must not be employed in any industrial
-- src:2666 | undertaking which the Minister by notification in the Gazette
-- src:2667 | declares to be an industrial undertaking in which a young person
-- src:2668 | must not be employed.
@ref s 69 (src:2665-2668)
GIVEN `the answer of s 67A "young person"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette declared the undertaking to be one in which a young person must not be employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 72(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69 the young person may be employed in the undertaking` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks of a young person
        IF `the answer of s 67A "young person"` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a young person is the answer of s 67A "young person", which was not given
        IF `the answer of s 67A "young person"` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 72(1) says sections 68 and 69 do not apply to this employment
        IF `the answer of s 72(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A young person must not be employed in any industrial undertaking which the Minister by notification in the Gazette declares"
        IF `the Minister has by notification in the Gazette declared the undertaking to be one in which a young person must not be employed` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is of an industrial undertaking which the Minister has declared
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 71(2): "Any person contravening any such order shall be guilty of an offence".  The order sets a minimum
-- rate of salary (an input); paying less than it is the contravention.
-- src:2691 | (2) Any person contravening any such order shall be guilty of an
-- src:2692 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2693 | $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to
-- src:2694 | both, and for a second or subsequent offence to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2695 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:2696 | both.
@ref s 71(2) (src:2691-2696)
GIVEN `the minimum rate of salary prescribed by the order` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the salary paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(2) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the minimum rate of salary prescribed by the order`
    WHEN JUST minimum THEN
        IF `the salary paid` LESS THAN minimum
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is contravening an order; paying the minimum or more is not a contravention of the order
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the order is not given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@ref s 71(2) (src:2691-2696)
GIVEN `it is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
`s 71(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `it is a second or subsequent offence`
    THEN `Penalty on conviction` WITH
            `least fine in dollars` IS 0
            `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 10000
            `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 24
    ELSE `Penalty on conviction` WITH
            `least fine in dollars` IS 0
            `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
            `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

-- s 73 (second limb): "a child or young person must not be employed as a workman under any circumstances or
-- under any conditions which may be prohibited by the Minister by regulations made under this Act."  Read as: the
-- circumstances and conditions are those the Minister has prohibited (reading 1, fork F14); the regulation-making
-- first limb is a power and has no function here.
-- src:2722 | 73. The Minister may make regulations for regulating the
-- src:2723 | employment of children in any occupation and a child or young
-- src:2724 | person must not be employed as a workman under any circumstances
-- src:2725 | or under any conditions which may be prohibited by the Minister by
-- src:2726 | regulations made under this Act.
@ref s 73 (src:2722-2726)
GIVEN `the answer of s 2(1) "workman"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a child or a young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has prohibited by regulations the circumstances or the conditions of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73 the child or young person may be employed as a workman` MEANS
    IF `the person is a child or a young person`
       AND `the answer of s 2(1) "workman"` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the Minister has prohibited by regulations the circumstances or the conditions of the employment`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a child or young person must not be employed as a workman under any circumstances"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is of employment as a workman in circumstances or on conditions the Minister has prohibited by regulations
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 74: "Any person who employs a child or young person in contravention of the provisions of this Part or any
-- of the regulations made under this Part and any parent or guardian who knowingly or negligently suffers or
-- permits such employment shall be guilty of an offence".
-- src:2730 | 74. Any person who employs a child or young person in
-- src:2731 | contravention of the provisions of this Part or any of the
-- src:2736 | regulations made under this Part and any parent or guardian who
-- src:2737 | knowingly or negligently suffers or permits such employment shall
-- src:2738 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:2739 | exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years
-- src:2740 | or to both, except in the case where a child or young person suffers
-- src:2741 | serious injury or death resulting from any breach of the provisions of
-- src:2742 | this Part or any regulations made under this Part the offender shall be
-- src:2743 | punished with a fine of $5,000 and shall also be liable to
-- src:2744 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years.
@ref s 74 (src:2730-2744)
GIVEN `the person employed a child or young person in contravention of the provisions of this Part or of the regulations made under it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a parent or guardian who knowingly or negligently suffered or permitted such employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74 the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person employed a child or young person in contravention of the provisions of this Part or of the regulations made under it`
       OR `the person is a parent or guardian who knowingly or negligently suffered or permitted such employment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is employing a child or young person in contravention of this Part or of the regulations, or as a parent or guardian knowingly or negligently suffering or permitting such employment
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 74: the penalty: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- both, except in the case where a child or young person suffers serious injury or death resulting from any
-- breach ... the offender shall be punished with a fine of $5,000 and shall also be liable to imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 2 years."  Serious injury or death: the fine is exactly $5,000.
@ref s 74 (src:2730-2744)
GIVEN `the child or young person suffered serious injury or death resulting from a breach of this Part or of the regulations made under it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
`s 74 the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the child or young person suffered serious injury or death resulting from a breach of this Part or of the regulations made under it`
    THEN `Penalty on conviction` WITH
            `least fine in dollars` IS 5000
            `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
            `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 24
    ELSE `Penalty on conviction` WITH
            `least fine in dollars` IS 0
            `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
            `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 24

-- s 75: "A child or young person in respect of whom any of the offences mentioned in this Part has been
-- committed may be brought before a Youth Court and the Court, if satisfied that the child or young person
-- requires care or protection, may exercise ... all or any of the powers conferred by section 54 of the
-- Children and Young Persons Act 1993."
-- src:2749 | 75. A child or young person in respect of whom any of the offences
-- src:2750 | mentioned in this Part has been committed may be brought before a
-- src:2751 | Youth Court and the Court, if satisfied that the child or young person
-- src:2752 | requires care or protection, may exercise with respect to that child or
-- src:2753 | young person all or any of the powers conferred by section 54 of the
-- src:2754 | Children and Young Persons Act 1993.
@ref s 75 (src:2749-2754)
GIVEN `an offence mentioned in this Part has been committed in respect of the child or young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75 the child or young person may be brought before a Youth Court` MEANS
    IF `an offence mentioned in this Part has been committed in respect of the child or young person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section is for a child or young person in respect of whom an offence mentioned in this Part has been committed
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 75 (src:2749-2754)
GIVEN `an offence mentioned in this Part has been committed in respect of the child or young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Youth Court is satisfied that the child or young person requires care or protection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75 the Youth Court may exercise the powers conferred by section 54 of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993` MEANS
    IF NOT `an offence mentioned in this Part has been committed in respect of the child or young person`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section is for "A child or young person in respect of whom any of the offences mentioned in this Part has been committed"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the Youth Court is satisfied that the child or young person requires care or protection`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court, if satisfied that the child or young person requires care or protection, may exercise"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
